// The correlated-driver member of the 0919 family: a DRIVER predicate joined
// on the anchor-shared var takes a different evaluation path than the
// standalone read, one where the same-step guard check is keyed by the
// DRIVER's value rather than the anchor row's.
//
// With a single event per step the driver pins `x` to the current event's
// server, so the foreign-mismatch trap of 0919 cannot fire here — this case
// is the OVER-CONSTRAINT control for that path: a MATCHING same-step
// heartbeat (@10, streak seeded at the same step) must still PERMIT once the
// guard check is keyed. @20 pins the no-anchor deny for a foreign server.
//
// Expected verdicts are in expected_1.out.
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Heartbeat",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    exists (x: String). (
        Drupe::Action::"Heartbeat"::request{ input.server: x }
        && (Drupe::Action::"Heartbeat"::request{ input.server: x }
            since within 1h
            Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.server: x })
    )
};
